[
    {
        "content": "<p>As a heavy user of the (fantastic!) <code>try?</code> tactic i sometimes see suggestions like<br>\n<a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/xWTqvw4_mRaEVcEB16N3IZ8b/image.png\">image.png</a><br>\nDo i understand correctly, that these proofs depend on the <code>proof</code> of a different theorem, not just its statement?</p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/xWTqvw4_mRaEVcEB16N3IZ8b/image.png\" title=\"image.png\"><img data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1062x152\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/xWTqvw4_mRaEVcEB16N3IZ8b/image.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><p>Sometimes it is reassuring to know that there exists a proof, but i would't ever want to depend on the proof of another theorem (and using the theorem in grind instead sometimes doesn't work!). If i ever refactor a proof, i dont want it to be able to transitively break stuff downwards.</p>\n<p>If so, is there a way to let <code>try?</code> try just as hard, as if it wouldn't have found these proofs?<br>\nI feel like it often is content with these and doesn't look further for a \"proper\" proof, which is a bit frustrating</p>",
        "id": 577601742,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1772746219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That seems fishy indeed. Unless <code>from_lex</code> is what you're proving?</p>",
        "id": 577607368,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1772748526
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>no, <code>from_lex</code> is an entirely different theorem in the same file</p>",
        "id": 577607531,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1772748590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe this is a different situation but I also sometimes see cases where the suggestion looks like <code>grind only [foo, bar, #wefoiwe, #234234]</code> and have never spent a moment asking or looking what those CSS-color-looking hash suggestions are but removing them has (in the cases I see) always resulted in a working grind call. Obviously I should have kept an <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> around, maybe I have one somewhere...</p>",
        "id": 577619415,
        "sender_full_name": "Julian Berman",
        "timestamp": 1772754482
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i think the hashes have something to do with local assumptions</p>",
        "id": 577619720,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1772754665
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And most often there is also a proof shown without the hashes</p>",
        "id": 577619789,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1772754713
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have thought of suggesting that <code>grind?</code> output be ordered by if they contain stable hashes and/or interactive mode. Still not sure in general how the hashes work, is it still too early for docs on these?</p>\n<p>I've also run into situations where it suggests an invalid hash, but I was deep enough in CSLib that I didn't know how to immediately minimize.</p>",
        "id": 577626200,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1772758165
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/UGLlN_uISDLXVXHljJ-GhfQI/image.png\">image.png</a><br>\nNow its referring to a simp? <span aria-label=\"eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f440\" role=\"img\" title=\"eyes\">:eyes:</span></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/UGLlN_uISDLXVXHljJ-GhfQI/image.png\" title=\"image.png\"><img data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1390x164\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/UGLlN_uISDLXVXHljJ-GhfQI/image.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div>",
        "id": 577707078,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1772791242
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span> <br>\nCan you maybe provide some of the reasoning behind allowing <code>try?</code> these proofs?</p>",
        "id": 578911381,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1773319397
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’d say that this is simply a bug. As always, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a>’s are appreciated :-)</p>",
        "id": 582761799,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1774952553
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The following is incomplete - <br>\ni managed to produce a (for the automation) nontrivial subproof but i can't get <code>try?</code> to find the subproof.<br>\nBut i know that this definitely still is a problem, at least on <code>Lean 4.29.0-rc2</code> since i have a reproducer of the usage of <code>_simp_1_5</code> together with <code>_proof_1_1</code> deep into my project.</p>\n<p>Maybe someone can modify this to get lucky with the lemma filter:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma_with_subproof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">solve_by_elim</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2_0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2_0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: lemma_with_subproof._proof_1_1 (this : Leq 1 0) : False -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma_with_subproof</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">proof_1_1</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- can't get `try?` to find the lemma here for reproduction</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">lemma_with_subproof</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">proof_1_1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n\n\n\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: Lean 4.29.0-rc2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Target: arm64-apple-darwin24.6.0 macOS</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">version</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 582788854,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1774960716
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is surpisingly hard to produce a nontrivial subproof, since lean will automatically extract <code>sorry</code>s and <code>axiom</code>s as hypothesis of the subproof</p>",
        "id": 582789641,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1774960868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and if one puts a <code>have</code> it sometimes also gets put as an hypothesis, even if fully proved</p>",
        "id": 582789828,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1774960920
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh heck no, it depends on using the module system smh</p>",
        "id": 582801174,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1774963707
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> <span aria-label=\"tada\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f389\" role=\"img\" title=\"tada\">:tada:</span></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- leaving out module will produce a `[apply] grind =&gt; sorry` at the `grind`+suggestions` instead (as expected)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LibrarySuggestions</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Default</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma_with_subproof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">solve_by_elim</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2_0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2_0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: lemma_with_subproof._proof_1_1 (this : Leq 1 0) : False -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma_with_subproof</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">proof_1_1</span>\n\n\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: Try these:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [apply] grind only [lemma_with_subproof._proof_1_1]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [apply] grind =&gt; instantiate only [lemma_with_subproof._proof_1_1]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Leq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind?</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">suggestions</span>\n\n\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: Lean 4.29.0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Target: x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">version</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
